VERDICT: PASS
===========================================================================
  `ipv6 traffic-filter v6glob` issued in GLOBAL config mode filters traffic
  on a port that carries NO per-port binding -- confirmed by reading the
  interface config back, which shows only switchport lines:
      interface port2.0.2 / switchport / switchport mode access
  and the global line present separately:
      ipv6 traffic-filter v6glob

  deny ipv6 2001:db8:7::/64 any   base 10/10 -> 0/10   (counters: 10 hits)
  permit ipv6 any any             base 10/10 -> 10/10

  This is the distinguishing behaviour of the case -- the filter reaches the
  port without being applied to it.

SCOPE NOT COVERED: the case also says "Ensure list is applied to a selection
of ports & static channel groups." Only the ingress port is instrumented for
traffic on this bench (one injection point, one capture point), and no static
channel group exists -- see the T881/885/889/890 note about the straddling LAG
not being buildable without recabling. The global-vs-per-port claim is proven;
"all ports and channel groups" is asserted by the platform, not measured here.
